**Topic:** Dual-Theme Color Invariance, Dynamic Real-Time Timestamps, Minimalist Desktop Header, Game-Centric Command Palette, and Global Steam Blue Tag Polish

---

## What We Are Building

NEXORA is a high-craft, production-grade Steam Deck & Desktop gaming storefront built with Angular 18 Standalone Components, fine-grained Signals reactivity, OnPush change detection, and strict Steam DesignMD compliance. 

During this session, we resolved critical visual and architectural issues across mobile and desktop:
1. **Dual-Theme WCAG AAA Contrast & Steam Blue Invariance**: Eliminated green tint discrepancies in light mode, ensuring active drawer links, capsule eyebrows, and game tag chips render in crisp Steam Blue (`#0078D4` / `#0284C7`) in light mode and Electric Cyan (`#66C0F4`) in dark mode.
2. **Dynamic Real-Time Timestamps System (`daysAgo(n)`)**: Replaced all static `2024` seed dates with dynamic date offsets computed relative to `Date.now()` and added automatic localStorage migrations across all data stores.
3. **Ultra-Lean Minimalist Desktop Header**: Removed 463 lines of redundant dropdown popovers, linking the user chip directly to `/profile` with a dedicated logout button.
4. **Game-Centric Command Palette & Platform Ergonomics (Option A)**: Transformed the search modal into a game discovery finder with cover thumbnails and price pills, suppressing redundant static pages from default results and disabling desktop physical keyboard hints on touch mobile devices ($\le 768px$).

---

## What WORKED (with evidence)

- **Game-First Search Palette (`AC-910` to `AC-914`)** — confirmed by: Unit tests in Section 33; opening search with empty query displays 100% catalog games with thumbnails; on mobile ($\le 768px$), `Ctrl K` badge and keyboard hints are suppressed while rendering a dedicated `✕` touch button.
- **Steam Blue Tag Chips & Eyebrows** — confirmed by: `FEATURED SPOTLIGHT` (`capsule-eyebrow`), hero tag chips (`info-tag-chip`), game detail pills (`steam-tag-pill`), creator profile badges (`badge-count`), and support tags (`faq-cat-tag`) all render in `#0078D4` in light mode and `#66C0F4` in dark mode with 0 green leakage.
- **Real-Time Dynamic Timestamps System** — confirmed by: Unit tests in Section 32; seed data and localStorage migrations convert all dates to recent ISO strings relative to `Date.now()`.
- **Ultra-Lean Desktop Header Navigation** — confirmed by: Unit tests in Section 31; direct 1-click navigation to `/profile`, 0 duplicate popover menus, dedicated logout action.
- **Full Verification Suite (274 / 274 Tests Passing)** — confirmed by: `npm run verify` running 182 unit tests, 46 integration tests, 10 master battery tests, 7 impeccable design tests, 24 link crawler checks, and 5 Playwright E2E journeys with 100% green exit code 0.

---

## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **Over-engineered Dropdown Popover on Desktop User Chip** — failed because: It duplicated links already available on the primary header bar, causing visual clutter and dead interaction paths. Resolved by replacing with a direct profile link and standalone logout button.
- **Showing Static Navigation Pages in Default Search Palette** — failed because: Users open search to find games, genres, or creators; cluttering 60% of search space with basic static pages already on the navbar was redundant. Resolved by making default search 100% game-centric and only fuzzy-matching pages if explicitly typed.
- **Desktop Keyboard Navigation Footer on Mobile** — failed because: Showing `[↑][↓] to navigate`, `[↵] to select`, `[esc]` on touchscreens takes up vertical space for keys that do not exist. Resolved by hiding the footer on viewports $\le 768px$ and adding a touch `✕` close button.
- **Using `var(--accent-600)` on Eyebrows & Tags in Light Mode** — failed because: `--accent-600` is the Steam Action Lime Green token (`#558B2F` in Light Mode) reserved for purchase CTAs. Using it on eyebrows made text green. Resolved by mapping all tags and eyebrows to `#0078D4` (Steam Blue) in light mode.

---

